#. Plugin Name of the plugin
#: customs.php
msgid "Customs - EU Import Duty for WooCommerce"
msgstr ""

#. Plugin URI of the plugin
#: customs.php
msgid "https://plogins.com/plogins-customs/"
msgstr ""

#. Description of the plugin
#: customs.php
msgid "Estimate and add the EU flat import duty (from 1 July 2026) as a clear checkout line for parcels shipped into the EU from outside it."
msgstr ""

#. Author of the plugin
#: customs.php
msgid "WPPoland.com"
msgstr ""

#. Author URI of the plugin
#: customs.php
msgid "https://wppoland.com"
msgstr ""

#: customs.php:48
msgid "Customs - EU Import Duty for WooCommerce requires WooCommerce to be active."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/ProductFields.php:35
msgid "Customs tariff code"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/ProductFields.php:37
msgid "Optional. Products sharing a code count as one EU import duty line. Leave empty to group by category."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/ProductFields.php:38
msgid "e.g. 6109 (T-shirts)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/ProductFields.php:45
msgid "Country of origin"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/ProductFields.php:47
msgid "Where the goods were made. Products with the same tariff line but a different origin count as separate duty lines. Leave on the store default to use the one set under WooCommerce, EU Import Duty."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/ProductFields.php:48
msgid "Store default"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/ProductFields.php:53
msgid "Outside the 3 EUR duty"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/ProductFields.php:54
msgid "Tick for goods that claim a preferential tariff, for example under a trade agreement, and are not imported under IOSS. They add no duty line. Their value still counts toward the goods-value threshold."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:52
#: src/Admin/Settings.php:53
#: src/Admin/Settings.php:114
msgid "EU Import Duty"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:93
msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:102
msgid "You do not have permission to manage these settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:117
msgid "From 1 July 2026 until 1 July 2028 the EU charges a temporary customs duty of 3 EUR per item on goods sold in distance sales and shipped into the EU from outside it, in consignments up to the goods-value threshold, with or without IOSS. Goods imported without IOSS that claim a preferential tariff are not covered; tick \"Outside the 3 EUR duty\" on those products. An item is goods sharing the same tariff classification, description and origin; the plugin counts one item per distinct tariff line and country of origin. How the estimate reaches the shopper is set under \"Who pays the duty\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:121
msgid "Settings saved."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:130
msgid "Enable duty estimate"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:134
msgid "Add the EU import duty line to qualifying carts."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:139
msgid "Legal period"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:143
msgid "Only apply the duty between 1 July 2026 and 1 July 2028"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:145
msgid "Council Regulation (EU) 2026/382, Article 2 sets this period, so outside it no duty line is added. Untick only if the period is extended."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:149
msgid "Who pays the duty"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:154
msgid "Charge it at checkout (DDP): the duty is added to the order total as its own pre-tax line."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:155
msgid "Show it as an estimate only (DAP): the shopper sees the amount but it is not added to the total, because it is paid on delivery."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:156
msgid "Absorb it: the shopper sees and pays nothing extra, and the amount is recorded on the order for your records."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:167
msgid "In the Cart and Checkout Blocks an estimate is shown on the order confirmation and in the order emails, not in the cart."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:172
msgid "Duty per tariff line (EUR)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:175
msgid "EU rule: 3 EUR per item (temporary, until 1 July 2028). The plugin treats each distinct tariff line as one item."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:179
msgid "Goods-value threshold (EUR)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:182
msgid "The duty applies only when the cart goods value is at or below this amount. EU rule: 150 EUR."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:186
msgid "Store currency per 1 EUR"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: store currency code.
#: src/Admin/Settings.php:192
#, php-format
msgid "Used to convert the EUR amounts into your store currency (%s). Leave at 1 if you sell in EUR."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:198
msgid "Store origin country"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:201
msgid "Use WooCommerce base country"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:214
msgid "Where parcels ship from. The duty only applies when this is outside the EU customs territory. Ceuta and Melilla are outside it: a Spanish store address in the province of Ceuta or Melilla, or with a postcode starting 51 or 52, counts as outside the EU."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:218
msgid "Default country of origin"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:221
msgid "Not set"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:234
msgid "Where your goods are made, for products without their own \"Country of origin\" on the Shipping tab. Under Delegated Regulation (EU) 2015/2446, Article 1(61), goods with the same tariff classification but a different declared origin are separate items, so the plugin counts each tariff line once per country of origin."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:238
msgid "Tariff line basis"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:243
msgid "One line per distinct product category (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:247
msgid "One line per distinct product"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:249
msgid "A tariff code set on a product always overrides this; products sharing a code count as one line."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:253
msgid "Count a subcategory under the category it sits in"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:257
msgid "Off: Other Products > Beads and Other Products > Pictures count as two lines. On: Books > Health and Books > Self improvement count as one. Which one is right depends on what your categories mean, so it is a choice rather than a rule. Give the products a tariff code and neither setting applies to them."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:264
msgid "Checkout line label"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:267
msgid "Leave empty to use the translated default shown in the field, so the line reads in the language of each shop."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:271
msgid "Apply tax to the duty"
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:275
msgid "Charge tax on the duty fee. Off by default, as customs duty is not normally taxed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:280
msgid "Save settings"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: products carrying a tariff code, 2: published products
#: src/Admin/Settings.php:385
#, php-format
msgid "Tariff codes found on %1$d of %2$d published products."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:395
msgid "The rest fall back to the category rule above. The field is called \"Customs tariff code\" and sits on the product's Shipping tab, which WooCommerce hides for products marked Virtual, and a code held in another plugin's field is not read here."
msgstr ""

#: src/Admin/Settings.php:410
msgid "No store origin country is set in WooCommerce, so the duty cannot be applied. Set a base country or choose an origin below."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: ISO country code.
#: src/Admin/Settings.php:418
#, php-format
msgid "Origin %s is inside the EU, so the duty will not be added (intra-EU shipments are excluded)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Cart/DutyFeeApplicator.php:81
#: src/Cart/DutyFeeApplicator.php:135
msgid "Not included in the total. Paid on delivery."
msgstr ""

#: src/Cart/DutyFeeApplicator.php:164
msgid "Absorbed by the store, not charged to the customer."
msgstr ""

#: src/Cart/DutyFeeApplicator.php:165
msgid "Shown to the customer as paid on delivery, not charged."
msgstr ""

